course: dictionary
lesson: 15350
title: Solidification: from liquid to solid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A noun can name a change. Solidification is the change of a liquid into a solid. Look for clues in the words around it: «Overnight, the water in the ice tray went through solidification and became solid ice.» Water that turns solid after a cold night has solidified, so solidification must mean becoming solid.
explain: Scientists use the word for the same change in many places. «As the lava cooled, its solidification turned it into hard black rock.» Lava is a hot liquid rock, and when it cools it becomes solid, so the clue is cooled and hard black rock.
explain: The word can also be used in a different way. «After weeks of talking, the team's plan reached solidification and nobody wanted to change it.» Here a plan is not a liquid. It means the plan became firm and fixed, like an opinion that has set.
fact: Solidification means the change of a liquid into a solid.
fact: Solidification is another word for freezing when a liquid becomes solid because it gets colder.
fact: Water freezes at 0 °C (32 °F), and that is when its solidification begins.
fact: Lava's solidification makes igneous rocks, and chocolate sets by solidification.
exercise: «Overnight, the water in the ice tray went through solidification.» What does solidification mean here? | Ice melting into water | A liquid turning into a gas | Water flowing faster down a slope | *The change of a liquid into a solid
exercise: «After weeks of talking, the team's plan reached solidification.» In this sentence, what does solidification suggest? | *The plan became firmer and more fixed | The plan became lighter and easier to carry | The plan was forgotten by everyone | The plan was thrown away
exercise: In science, solidification is another word for which process? | *Freezing | Evaporating | Boiling | Melting
test: When melted wax hardens again, which change of state is this? | Evaporation | Melting | *Solidification
test: «Lava's solidification makes which kind of rock?» | *Igneous | Metamorphic | Sedimentary
exam: At what temperature does water freeze, so that its solidification begins? | 100 °C | 50 °C | *0 °C | -20 °C
